NAME
     lsof - what files are open

SYNOPSIS
     lsof [-p PID] [-u USER] [-c NAME] [-t]
     fuser FILE...

DESCRIPTION
     lsof prints a line per open file: the process, its user, the
     descriptor number, the kind of thing it is and its name. Called as
     fuser it prints the processes that have a given file open.

OPTIONS
     -p PID    only that process
     -u USER   only that user's
     -c NAME   only processes whose command begins with NAME
     -t        only the process ids, for feeding to kill

SEE ALSO
     ps(1), netstat(1), /proc in procfs
